# ===========================================================================
#  Line ending policy
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
#  --------------------
#  Without it, Git's behaviour depends on each developer's core.autocrlf
#  setting, and the same commit can look like a whole-file rewrite on someone
#  else's machine. The default state of this repo was already producing
#  "LF will be replaced by CRLF" warnings on every checkout.
#
#  THE POLICY
#  ----------
#  Store LF in the repository, always. Check out CRLF on Windows for files
#  Windows tooling expects to be CRLF. This gives:
#    * identical bytes in the object database regardless of who committed,
#    * no phantom whole-file diffs when a line-ending preference differs,
#    * LF on Linux/macOS and in CI, so shell scripts and CI scripts behave.
#
#  C++ sources are listed as text=auto rather than forced to CRLF: modern
#  MSVC, Clang and GCC all handle LF correctly, and leaving them LF keeps
#  diffs clean when the same file is edited on either platform.
# ===========================================================================

# Default: normalise text files to LF in the repository, honour platform
# conventions on checkout.
* text=auto eol=lf

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  Windows-only scripts: CRLF, because cmd.exe mis-parses LF-only batch files
#  (a stray LF inside a .bat can silently truncate a line).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  Files that must stay binary. Marking these prevents Git from attempting to
#  normalise them, which corrupts shaders, textures and imported assets.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.dll   binary
*.lib   binary
*.exe   binary
*.pdb   binary
*.obj   binary
*.cso   binary
*.dxil  binary
*.spv   binary
*.dds   binary
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.tga   binary
*.fbx   binary
*.glb   binary

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  Generated artefacts that should never be committed, even by accident.
#  This is a second line of defence: .gitignore covers the build trees, but
#  these patterns catch the same extensions anywhere else in the tree.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
build/**     text=auto
*.log        text
*.user      text